1
00:00:04,140 --> 00:00:05,500
An agent can read a page.

2
00:00:05,821 --> 00:00:07,321
But which address can it connect to?

3
00:00:08,862 --> 00:00:10,882
Cloudflare added a new web fetch tool.

4
00:00:11,663 --> 00:00:14,244
We tested the published code with local
responses.

5
00:00:15,064 --> 00:00:17,525
Twenty seven cases gave the specified
results.

6
00:00:18,605 --> 00:00:20,986
The policy rejected private address forms.

7
00:00:21,406 --> 00:00:24,227
It examined each redirect target before
the next fetch call.

8
00:00:24,727 --> 00:00:27,848
But a permitted hostname does not
establish the destination address.

9
00:00:28,829 --> 00:00:31,129
This policy does not resolve domain names.

10
00:00:32,110 --> 00:00:33,970
Network controls need their own test.

11
00:00:34,711 --> 00:00:36,171
The runtime also matters.

12
00:00:36,431 --> 00:00:38,472
Workers can use different network
connections.

13
00:00:38,752 --> 00:00:42,593
A private network binding changes which
services an application can contact.

14
00:00:42,994 --> 00:00:44,854
A second change affects page conversion.

15
00:00:45,214 --> 00:00:48,455
Cloudflare now streams converted Markdown
without a content length header.

16
00:00:48,896 --> 00:00:50,536
Our test used a smaller body limit.

17
00:00:50,576 --> 00:00:51,697
Eight bytes were accepted.

18
00:00:52,057 --> 00:00:54,258
Nine bytes were rejected, even without
that header.

19
00:00:55,098 --> 00:00:56,338
Use a small host list.

20
00:00:56,598 --> 00:00:58,399
Keep redirect checks and response limits.

21
00:00:58,679 --> 00:01:01,300
Examine the network configuration before
the agent connects.
